-modules on\nthe big <MATH_0008> site of <MATH_0009>. By\nModules on Sites, Definition <REF_0004>\nthere exists a <MATH_0010>-covering <MATH_0011> of <MATH_0012>\nsuch that each of the restrictions\n<MATH_0013> has a global presentation\n<MATH_0014>\nfor some index sets <MATH_0015> and <MATH_0016>. We claim that this implies\nthat <MATH_0017> is <MATH_0018>\nfor some quasi-coherent sheaf <MATH_0019> on <MATH_0020>. Namely,\nthis is clear for the direct sums\n<MATH_0021>\nand\n<MATH_0022>.\nHence we see that <MATH_0023> is a\ncokernel of a map <MATH_0024>\nfor some quasi-coherent sheaves <MATH_0025>, <MATH_0026>\non <MATH_0027>. By the fully faithfulness of <MATH_0028> we see that\n<MATH_0029> for some map of quasi-coherent sheaves\n<MATH_0030> on <MATH_0031>. Then it is\nclear that\n<MATH_0032>\nas claimed.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nSince <MATH_0033> lives on all of the category\n<MATH_0034> we see that\n<MATH_0035>\nas <MATH_0036>-modules on <MATH_0037>.\nHence, using fully faithfulness again we get canonical isomorphisms\n<MATH_0038>\nof quasi-coherent modules over <MATH_0039>. We omit the verification\nthat these satisfy the cocycle condition. Since they do we see by\neffectivity of descent for quasi-coherent sheaves and the covering\n<MATH_0040> (Proposition <REF_0005>)\nthat there exists a quasi-coherent sheaf <MATH_0041> on <MATH_0042>\nwith <MATH_0043> compatible\nwith the given descent data. In other words we are given\n<MATH_0044>-module isomorphisms\n<MATH_0045>\nwhich agree over <MATH_0046>. Hence, since\n<MATH_0047> is\na sheaf (Modules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0006>),\nwe conclude that\nthere is a morphism of <MATH_0048>-modules <MATH_0049>\nrecovering the isomorphisms <MATH_0050> above. Hence this is an isomorphism\nand we win.\n\n<STRUCT_0005><STRUCT_0006>\nThe case of the sites <MATH_0051> and <MATH_0052> is proved in the\nexact same manner.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:592cad22d717dd49f7a6cd2d80e2c097c2ef2ab2895d303faa40e14c47a95991", "unit_id":